Is Mr Bouchard going to be here ?

996
01:14:30,342 --> 01:14:33,341
Please , please . I have a statement to make .

997
01:14:33,385 --> 01:14:36,635
- Was there an explosion ? - How many people are missing ?

998
01:14:36,681 --> 01:14:39,301
Late today , due to a minor disturbance ,

999
01:14:39,349 --> 01:14:42,684
there was a pressure failure in one of the tunnels -

1000
01:14:42,728 --> 01:14:44,767
a major attraction at the park .

1001
01:14:44,812 --> 01:14:47,765
We estimate that 30 to 40 people

1002
01:14:47,815 --> 01:14:50,601
were in the process of being evacuated

1003
01:14:50,650 --> 01:14:55,194
when the watertight safety doors temporarily delayed their exit .

1004
01:14:55,240 --> 01:14:58,026
We 're working right now to release them

1005
01:14:58,075 --> 01:15:00,744
under the safest possible circumstances .

1006
01:15:00,786 --> 01:15:04,035
Seven visitors were also injured in our beach area .

1007
01:15:04,080 --> 01:15:07,497
- That 's all . Give me a break . - What about a shark ?

1008
01:15:07,542 --> 01:15:11,325
- I 'll let you know as I know more . - A very large shark ...

1009
01:15:11,379 --> 01:15:14,083
That 's all . There is no more .

1010
01:15:14,131 --> 01:15:16,040
( Woman ) When will this be fixed ?

1011
01:15:16,092 --> 01:15:18,760
( Guide ) I 'm sure they 're working on it .

1012
01:15:18,803 --> 01:15:22,170
Stay together to keep warm . I know you 're cold .

1013
01:15:22,221 --> 01:15:27,464
Stay together , take shallow breaths and concentrate on your breathing .

1014
01:15:44,701 --> 01:15:47,071
Well , any sign of mother ?

1015
01:15:48,454 --> 01:15:49,734
OK , then .

1016
01:15:49,788 --> 01:15:53,489
Where did the animal hide the first time ?

1017
01:15:55,084 --> 01:15:56,414
Uh ...

1018
01:15:58,255 --> 01:16:00,461
filtration pipe .

1019
01:16:00,506 --> 01:16:02,498
Opposite side of the lagoon .

1020
01:16:02,548 --> 01:16:07,211
Brody , is there an access hatch , a backwash gate ?

1021
01:16:08,264 --> 01:16:13,304
Heavy grillwork . Keeps the pumps clear when we back-flush that system .

1022
01:16:13,352 --> 01:16:16,685
Why ? What do you want to do ? Get that thing back in ?

1023
01:16:16,729 --> 01:16:18,686
He 's a bright lad .

1024
01:16:18,731 --> 01:16:23,477
Yes . Jack and I are going to lure him back into the pipe ,

1025
01:16:23,527 --> 01:16:27,525
close the gates and then dispose of him at our leisure .

1026
01:16:27,573 --> 01:16:31,867
Meanwhile , you can weld your patch and then evacuate the civilians .

1027
01:16:31,909 --> 01:16:35,195
What if she doesn 't want to go back in ?

1028
01:16:35,247 --> 01:16:39,541
I think we can pretty much guarantee she 'll want to go back in .

1029
01:16:39,583 --> 01:16:41,741
- Right , Jack ? - Sure .

1030
01:16:41,793 --> 01:16:44,463
Just how are you going to guarantee that ?

1031
01:16:46,090 --> 01:16:48,082
Live bait .

1032
01:16:48,133 --> 01:16:51,751
( Man ) We 're ready to move out over the tunnel now .

1033
01:16:51,802 --> 01:16:53,761
( Mike ) Let 's go .

1034
01:17:04,398 --> 01:17:06,520
L-I 'll be in the Control Room .

1035
01:17:06,566 --> 01:17:08,974
I 'll go with you .

1036
01:17:10,737 --> 01:17:13,109
( Man ) Give me that . I 'll store it over here .

1037
01:17:13,155 --> 01:17:14,615
( Man ) No , I got it .

1038
01:17:17,327 --> 01:17:18,405
( Technician ) Yeah , we 're on top of it .

1039
01:17:18,451 --> 01:17:20,575
OK . Thanks .

1040
01:17:28,837 --> 01:17:30,829
Now , where 's that damn fish ?

1041
01:17:33,590 --> 01:17:35,548
There . I 've got him .

1042
01:17:35,593 --> 01:17:38,130
( Technician ) Sorry , it 's the dolphins .

1043
01:17:40,889 --> 01:17:43,595
Babies , stay out of it , please .

1044
01:17:43,642 --> 01:17:46,595
... and I 've rigged a lifeline .

1045
01:17:46,645 --> 01:17:50,772
Just let the pumps push you out and use the rope to pull yourself back .

1046
01:17:50,815 --> 01:17:52,191
Right .

1047
01:17:53,568 --> 01:17:57,184
And why don 't I do all the filming ?

1048
01:17:57,238 --> 01:18:01,151
I want both cameras . We need the coverage . Come on , Jack !

1049
01:18:01,199 --> 01:18:03,156
This isn 't a picnic .

1050
01:18:03,200 --> 01:18:07,199
This film is a bloody retirement annuity .

1051
01:18:07,247 --> 01:18:10,081
I 'd feel better if you did just the one thing .

1052
01:18:10,124 --> 01:18:12,081
( Laughs ) What 's the matter ?

1053
01:18:12,126 --> 01:18:14,119
Getting cold feet ?

1054
01:18:21,718 --> 01:18:24,635
OK , Bob . Hold it about right there .

1055
01:18:24,679 --> 01:18:28,298
- We 're right over the tunnel . - OK , we 're all set .

1056
01:18:28,349 --> 01:18:30,841
( Mike ) ' Tell FitzRoyce we 're in position . '

1057
01:18:30,893 --> 01:18:33,301
FitzRoyce , you can go now .

1058
01:18:58,543 --> 01:19:03,251
( Technician ) They 're testing the lifeline to see if it 's secure .

1059
01:19:22,983 --> 01:19:27,027
( Calvin ) ' They 're spreadin ' some chum . You know , fish oil and blood .

1060
01:19:27,070 --> 01:19:29,987
' Then Jack 's gonna make some metallic sounds

1061
01:19:30,030 --> 01:19:33,446
' to attract her right down into that filtration pipe . '

1062
01:19:33,491 --> 01:19:35,319
Start the pumps .

1063
01:19:35,370 --> 01:19:37,491
You got it .

1064
01:19:42,709 --> 01:19:45,413
( Metal clanging )

1065
01:20:02,684 --> 01:20:05,011
( Clanging )

1066
01:21:06,868 --> 01:21:10,450
( Technician ) It 's in ! ( Calvin ) He 's got it !

1067
01:21:10,497 --> 01:21:12,572
All right . It 's locked .

1068
01:21:14,624 --> 01:21:16,748
It 's safe , Brody . Go for it .

1069
01:21:16,794 --> 01:21:18,704
OK , let 's go .

1070
01:22:10,592 --> 01:22:12,004
( Muffled scream )

1071
01:22:46,292 --> 01:22:49,626
( Technician ) ' This is Control . Is that patch in place ? '

1072
01:22:49,669 --> 01:22:51,415
Easy .

1073
01:23:01,306 --> 01:23:04,011
Let me help you with that , Dr Morgan .

1074
01:23:04,058 --> 01:23:05,966
Got it !

1075
01:23:08,270 --> 01:23:10,393
Now weld the son-of-a-bitch ...

1076
01:23:11,649 --> 01:23:14,186
( Calvin ) Kathryn , what are you doin ' ?

1077
01:23:14,234 --> 01:23:16,311
I 'm going down there .

1078
01:23:19,031 --> 01:23:20,488
You crazy ?

1079
01:23:20,531 --> 01:23:23,104
He needs eyes in the back of his head .

1080
01:23:28,121 --> 01:23:30,410
- Thanks , Fred . - All right .

1081
01:23:30,457 --> 01:23:32,615
Watch the tanks .

1082
01:23:32,667 --> 01:23:34,293
OK .

1083
01:23:37,922 --> 01:23:40,211
- Here are your fins . - Thanks .

1084
01:23:40,257 --> 01:23:42,713
Be careful down there now .

1085
01:23:57,356 --> 01:23:59,562
( Hinges creaking )

1086
01:24:29,134 --> 01:24:31,044
( Sighs ) You all right ?

1087
01:24:32,137 --> 01:24:34,047
Where 's Mr FitzRoyce ?

1088
01:24:34,097 --> 01:24:36,055
I have no idea .

1089
01:24:39,520 --> 01:24:41,144
( Man ) What 's goin ' on ?

1090
01:24:43,815 --> 01:24:45,014
Guv 'nor !

1091
01:24:45,276 --> 01:24:47,066
Guv 'nor !

1092
01:24:47,318 --> 01:24:49,940
Guv 'nor !

1093
01:24:50,030 --> 01:24:51,737
There 's no other way out ?

1094
01:24:51,781 --> 01:24:54,021
You don 't understand . This is it !

1095
01:24:54,074 --> 01:24:56,031
Have you looked ?

1096
01:24:56,076 --> 01:24:58,863
He didn 't come up .

1097
01:24:58,912 --> 01:25:02,328
Guv 'nor , you bloody bastard . Answer me !

1098
01:25:08,713 --> 01:25:11,631
We 'll suffocate the bitch . Shut down the pumps .

1099
01:25:11,674 --> 01:25:12,955
Are you sure ?

1100
01:25:13,009 --> 01:25:16,174
- Why don 't we blow it up ? - Listen , nephew .

1101
01:25:16,219 --> 01:25:20,299
A $ 2.5 million turbine 's not going up in smoke cos of a damn fish !

1102
01:25:20,348 --> 01:25:22,969
Now shut the pumps down !

1103
01:25:24,353 --> 01:25:26,641
( Mechanical whirring )

1104
01:25:26,688 --> 01:25:29,014
What 's happened ?

1105
01:25:29,066 --> 01:25:31,555
( Man ) They 've shut the pumps off .

1106
01:25:31,610 --> 01:25:36,437
( Sighs ) That 's all she needs . The gates can 't hold much longer .

1107
01:25:38,531 --> 01:25:42,612
( Sobbing ) Philip , pull the pin ! Pull the pin , Philip .

1108
01:26:08,767 --> 01:26:11,259
( Metallic clanking on monitor )

1109
01:26:17,567 --> 01:26:19,940
( Clanking )

1110
01:26:43,925 --> 01:26:46,082
( Clanking continues )

1111
01:27:05,319 --> 01:27:07,026
( Woman ) Look at that !

1112
01:27:13,994 --> 01:27:16,781
( Woman ) Jesus !

1113
01:27:16,829 --> 01:27:18,868
( Fred ) Oh , my God !

1114
01:27:18,956 --> 01:27:21,281
We gotta warn ' em . We gotta tell ' em !

1115
01:27:21,333 --> 01:27:24,203
Get ' em up ! It 's coming back . Get ' em up quick !

1116
01:27:24,252 --> 01:27:26,411
- Come on ! Hurry up ! - Come on !

1117
01:27:26,463 --> 01:27:27,626
Get ' em up !

1118
01:27:41,685 --> 01:27:43,760
- Come on , Mike . - Get out of there !

1119
01:27:50,527 --> 01:27:53,611
- Come on , Mike ! - ( Calvin ) ' Get ' em up ! '

1120
01:28:22,473 --> 01:28:24,679
( Muffled ) Come on !

1121
01:28:32,565 --> 01:28:34,724
( Squeaking )

1122
01:28:40,030 --> 01:28:41,857
( Squeaking )

1123
01:29:35,664 --> 01:29:37,455
( Muffled ) Pull the door !

1124
01:30:06,733 --> 01:30:09,522
How the hell did it get loose ?

1125
01:30:13,990 --> 01:30:16,445
Open the hatch !

1126
01:30:20,455 --> 01:30:22,696
( Fred ) Come on up , Mike . I gotcha .

1127
01:30:28,713 --> 01:30:31,083
Are you all right ?

1128
01:30:31,131 --> 01:30:33,834
Do we have pressure in those tunnels yet ?

1129
01:30:33,883 --> 01:30:36,969
- Affirmative . - Then get those people out .

1130
01:30:39,639 --> 01:30:42,556
Feel the air ! Can you feel the air ?

1131
01:30:42,601 --> 01:30:45,554
The water 's going down . The water 's going down !

1132
01:30:50,356 --> 01:30:53,143
Try to be calm . Don 't rush to the door .

1133
01:31:04,202 --> 01:31:06,112
( Man ) We 're saved !

1134
01:31:06,164 --> 01:31:08,285
( All talking and cheering )

1135
01:32:10,054 --> 01:32:12,509
( Muffled yelling , crunching )

1136
01:34:25,720 --> 01:34:27,628
Oh ! We did it !

1137
01:34:27,680 --> 01:34:30,349
The others , Mike . What about the others ?

1138
01:34:30,390 --> 01:34:32,466
Calvin made it . Lisa .

1139
01:34:32,517 --> 01:34:36,053
Mike . Mike ! The dolphins !

1140
01:34:37,188 --> 01:34:38,647
( Kay ) Cindy !

1141
01:34:38,690 --> 01:34:41,097
( Mike ) Cindy ! ( Kay ) Sandy !

1142
01:34:41,150 --> 01:34:44,684
- Come on ! Cindy ! - Cindy !

1143
01:34:44,736 --> 01:34:47,904
Oh , good girl . Sandy !

1144
01:34:47,947 --> 01:34:49,228
( Squeaks )

1145
01:34:49,282 --> 01:34:54,240
Sandy , come on , baby . Sandy , where are you ?

1146
01:34:54,287 --> 01:34:56,196
( Mike ) Sandy !

1147
01:34:57,456 --> 01:34:59,366
I hope she made it .

1148
01:35:01,377 --> 01:35:03,285
- Cindy , stay . - Sandy .

1149
01:35:03,337 --> 01:35:05,294
( Squeaks )

1150
01:35:06,882 --> 01:35:09,254
Sandy !

1151
01:35:09,300 --> 01:35:11,542
All right !

1152
01:35:23,355 --> 01:35:25,263
All right !

